      "type": "mini_coding",
      "title": "Limit each client with a token bucket",
      "description": "The editor holds the gateway's limiter (`main.go`) with key blocks missing, each marked by a `// [ ]` line; some pieces are wrong on purpose. Fill every line so that: each client has a bucket of `burst` tokens refilled at `rate` tokens per second and never above `burst`; a request spends a token or is refused with a wait until the next token; `Retry-After` is that wait in whole seconds rounded up; anonymous clients are keyed by their own address, taking X-Forwarded-For only when the peer is the load balancer (10.0.0.0/8) and then only its last entry; and `Evict` forgets buckets that are full again. Run plays timed requests through the limiter and prints each decision.",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "outcomes": [
        "traffic-control"
      ],
      "points": 30,
      "hints": [
        "Replay one client by hand: how many tokens does it have at each request, what caps them, and how long is it until the next whole token when there is none?",
        "Look at `math.Min`, `math.Ceil`, `netip.Prefix.Contains`, the last element of `strings.Split(...)`, and when a bucket is indistinguishable from a new one.",
        "A login limiter with the same shape: `tries = math.Min(5, tries + elapsed.Minutes()*0.5)`, refuse below 1 with `wait = (1 - tries) / 0.5` minutes, `Retry-After = ceil(seconds)`, and key by the user name plus the trusted client address."
